# Static-asset headers (Workers assets convention).
# HTML is never cached by the browser so a deploy reaches everyone on the next
# load; Next's hashed /_next/static files are immutable, and so are the site's
# content-hashed product captures under /site/captures/ (AMENDMENTS-SITE-NEWUSER
# §3.13). Only content-hashed files live there (site-captures.test.ts); other
# files under /site/ (share images, say) keep the default caching.
# Baseline security headers for every path ([AU] AMENDMENTS-AUDIT-2026-11 AU-5,
# audit SEC-3). Rules that match the same path are merged and a header two of them
# set is sent as "a, b", so no other rule of this file sets one of these five. A
# script-source policy is not here: it needs a report-only period first.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/site/captures/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
